# OSE Agent Playbook Source Pointers

## Purpose

Agent skills/playbooks should be OSE interfaces with source pointers, not free-floating vibes.

Each playbook tells an agent **how to play or adjudicate** a bounded part of Old School Essentials, and includes URL pointers for the Referee/runtime to look up the underlying book chunks when needed.

## Pointer shape

Use JoelClaw docs chunk URLs as the durable pointer:

```txt
https://joelclaw.com/api/docs/chunks/{chunkId}?lite=true&includeEmbedding=false
```

For deeper Referee-only lookup:

```txt
https://joelclaw.com/api/docs/chunks/{chunkId}?lite=false&includeEmbedding=false
```

Search pointer shape:

```txt
https://joelclaw.com/api/docs/search?q={encodedQuery}&perPage=5&semantic=false
```

Discovery:

```txt
https://joelclaw.com/api/docs
```

## Playbook metadata shape

A player-safe playbook should carry pointers, not raw book dumps:

```yaml
sourcePointers:
  - label: Thief skills
    docId: old-school-essentials-basic-rules-v1-4-a4d9608ea98b
    chunkId: old-school-essentials-basic-rules-v1-4-a4d9608ea98b:s127:n0
    url: https://joelclaw.com/api/docs/chunks/old-school-essentials-basic-rules-v1-4-a4d9608ea98b:s127:n0?lite=true&includeEmbedding=false
    visibility: referee-source/player-safe-summary
```

