  - URL: `https://joelclaw.com/api/docs/chunks/old-school-essentials-classic-fantasy-rules-tome-3751c5149a24:s659:n0?lite=true&includeEmbedding=false`

## Visibility rule

PlayerAgent playbooks should include:

- concise player-safe summaries,
- allowed action/interface guidance,
- source pointer IDs/URLs for audit,
- no raw full book chunks.

RefereeAgent playbooks may use deeper source lookup, but public/table output still gets only safe summaries and doc/chunk receipts.

## Runtime idea

When a PlayerAgent faces a situation, Referee provides only relevant playbooks:

```txt
PlayerAgent sees:
  - player-survival.md
  - class-thief.md
  - table-caller.md
  - current table state

PlayerAgent does not see:
  - raw OSE corpus
  - Referee hidden notes
  - other player private Brain repos
```

The URL pointers let the Referee/runtime refresh or verify a playbook against the book without giving every player mind direct corpus access.
